# PairUp Events - Cursor Rules

**Start here**: Read `AGENTS.md` (root directory) for the universal agent entry point and mandatory protocol.

This file contains project-specific rules and conventions for AI-assisted development.

## Key Locations

- **`AGENTS.md`** – Universal agent entry point (read this first!)
- **`Docs/architecture/`** – Factual project knowledge (component standards, Firebase patterns, testing)
- **`Docs/data-model.md`** – Firestore schema reference
- **`Docs/CHANGELOG.md`** – Project history and decision log
- **`.cursor/commands/`** – Cursor IDE commands (thin wrappers, see `.agents/` for actual instructions)

## Quick Navigation

- Component patterns → `Docs/architecture/component-standards.md`
- Firebase rules → `Docs/architecture/firebase-patterns.md`
- Testing → `Docs/architecture/testing-standards.md`
- Design system → `Docs/architecture/design-language.md`
- State management → `Docs/architecture/state-management.md`

All behavioral instructions for agents are now in AGENTS.md and `.agents/` directory.
